  "Negatives: 54 clips, about 0.1 h of non-wake audio. Zero observed false triggers gives only a rule-of-three upper bound of about 30 per hour; a multi-hour negative run is still needed.",
  "Latency is measured with snapshot polling (about 20 ms) and is relative to the clip, not to the end of the word \"Gideon\".",
  "Command grammar still refuses an STT period after the wake word (\"Hey Gideon. Mute.\") and STT misrecognitions (\"A gideon\", \"Gideons\", bare \"Gideon\"); this is recognition quality, not the wake path.",
